Milestone: Original startup branding and an infinite-battery remembered console
Dependencies: 08_POWER_LIFECYCLE, 09_NATIVE_SETTINGS, 10_DARK_ROOM
Purpose: Start first visits off, remember the switch and last cartridge through
  refresh, and play a familiar but original LCD startup only on actual power-on.

Tasks:
- [x] Review the supplied video's public metadata/thumbnail as visual reference.
- [x] Create original website logo/favicon and LCD artwork, without Nintendo assets.
- [x] Synthesize an original chime honoring volume/mute and bounded audio errors.
- [x] Keep first use and off-state cartridge insertion genuinely powered off.
- [x] Make the physical switch work even with an empty cartridge slot.
- [x] Persist checked switch intent and the last local cartridge.
- [x] Preserve existing game records through the v2 database upgrade.
- [x] Restore on/off intent on refresh without replaying the startup sequence.
- [x] Preserve battery-only cold boot, checkpoints, backups and failure recovery.
- [x] Exercise original startup, exact native resume and storage abort/migration.
- [x] Deploy and verify the live site before final public documentation.

Acceptance criteria:
- A fresh browser profile has dark LCD/LED and no emulator iframe.
- Inserting a cartridge while off cannot turn the switch on.
- Only actual off-to-on calls the original startup; refresh never does.
- Refresh retains an on console's cartridge and checked resume point.
- Refresh retains an off console without creating an emulator.
- Only the physical switch changes power intent; no battery/idle timeout exists.
- Power-on cold-boots battery saves, not an instant checkpoint.
- Aborted power persistence leaves previous state and a live game recoverable.
- Browser denial is explicit; local persistence is not an exported backup.
- Native settings stay at the top of the sidebar and preserve the live runtime.
- Technical verification/publication remain distinct from human visual approval.

